messages[12]{user,text}:
  user_1,[00:00] Hello, uh... is this Vikram from Omni Insurance?
  user_2,[00:04] Yes, hi Riya! This is Vikram, how can I help you today?
  user_1,[00:08] I... I was looking at my health policy, the one... the SH-2024... I think it's about to end?
  user_2,[00:12] Let me pull it up... [typing] ... okay, I see it here. Your policy actually expired on 30/08/2026.
  user_1,[00:18] Oh no, really? I didn't realize... [sighs] What does that mean for me now?
  user_2,[00:22] It means you’re no longer covered for new claims. You can renew or switch to a new plan.
  user_1,[00:27] Can I still get coverage for... like, an upcoming doctor appointment next week?
  user_2,[00:31] Unfortunately, once expired, any new services aren’t covered unless you renew first.
  user_1,[00:35] Hmm... okay. What’s the renewal process? Is it quick?
  user_2,[00:39] Yeah, we can do it over the phone. I’ll need a few details—your DOB, address, and payment method.
  user_1,[00:44] Sure, my DOB is 12/05/1990, address is 45 Greenfield Lane, Bangalore.
  user_2,[00:48] Got it. I’ll send you a renewal link via email after this call. Anything else?